  star-submit job for macros/MakeEventCutFlow_OO200.C over the SAME picoDst set as the
  PicoBinner production (xml/runPicoBinner_OO200_SDCC_template.xml): identical catalog
  query and 120-run whitelist. One output ROOT file per job; hadd them afterwards:
    hadd -f cutflow_OO200_all.root /star/data03/pwg/liggett/CutFlow_OO200/*_cutflow.root
  then plot on the laptop with macros/PlotEventCutFlow_OO200.C.

  Before submitting (on RCF, from the repo root): bin/libStPicoDst.so must exist (README,
  One-time build setup, step 1) and the output directory must exist:
    mkdir -p /star/data03/pwg/liggett/CutFlow_OO200 /star/data03/scratch/liggett/schedFiles/cutFlow_OO200 /star/data03/scratch/liggett/cutFlow_OO200/stdout_stderr
  Submit with:  rm -f CutFlow_OO200.zip; star-submit xml/runCutFlow_OO200_SDCC.xml
  (SUMS reuses an existing CutFlow_OO200.zip sandbox without repacking it, so after any
  change to macros/ or scripts/ the old zip must be deleted or the jobs run the old code.)
-->

